# DAE workflow (Disciplined Agentic Engineering)

Methodology repo: `tools/dae` — https://github.com/swingerman/disciplined-agentic-engineering

Use for non-trivial features: charter → ACs → Gherkin spec → plan → implement → verify.

## Claude Code (full toolkit)

```text
/plugin marketplace add swingerman/disciplined-agentic-engineering
/plugin install engineer@disciplined-agentic-engineering
/plugin install atdd@disciplined-agentic-engineering
```

Then run onboard once; per feature use checkpoints 0 → 8 from `tools/dae/README.md`.

## Cursor (this repo)

1. Copy or init `CHARTER.md` at repo root (architecture, layers, naming, test stance).
2. Create `features/NNN-short-name/` with `feature.md`, `acs.md`, `spec.md`, `plan.md`.
3. Implement only after human approves `spec.md` + architecture section of `plan.md`.
4. Two test streams where applicable: acceptance (Gherkin/scene tests) + unit (GUT/godot tests).

## Suggested feature folders for this game

- `001-core-triple-match` — select 3 tiles, clear, free-tile rules
- `002-level-01` — one shippable level + win screen
- `003-touch-ui` — HUD, score, progress, touch targets
- `004-aurora-port` — export constraints, input, packaging

Do not skip acceptance criteria for hackathon-mandatory behavior (touch-only, score/progress).
